# POLLY, walkthrough: MANUAL.md's "Writing a song", step by step, as written there (the steps' numbers below).
# Funk at 100 BPM: a beat 600 ms, a bar 2400 ms; the waits put each chord just after a bar line. Keys: F3 0, G3 2,
# A3 4, B3 6, C4 7, D4 9, E4 11, G4 14 (Am 4 7 11, F 0 4 7, C 7 11 14, G 2 6 9). Chords as expected: root * 100 +
# CH_* (maj 0, min 16), -1 no change. Pages: 0 HOME, 1-3 SONG, 4-5 LOOP. White keys w0..w15 are the manual's 1..16
# (w8: white key 9, L9).
wait 300
expect page 0
expect mode 0
expect rows 0
# ---- 1. Find a groove: KNOB 1 a style (Funk), PLAY, a chord of three keys: the band follows
turn K1 1
expect tempo 100
tap PLAY
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
wait 100
key 4 up
key 7 up
key 11 up
expect chord_root 9
expect chord_type 16
wait 100
shot 1_groove.png
# ---- 2. Write your verse: REC, Am F C G a bar each, REC: loop L9, the band plays it round; name it: ARP, SELECT to
# page 2, NAME: Verse
tap REC
expect take 2
wait 2128
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
wait 100
key 4 up
key 7 up
key 11 up
wait 2288
key 0 down
key 4 down
key 7 down
wait 100
key 0 up
key 4 up
key 7 up
shot 2_verse_take.png
wait 2288
key 7 down
key 11 down
key 14 down
wait 100
key 7 up
key 11 up
key 14 up
wait 2288
key 2 down
key 6 down
key 9 down
wait 100
key 2 up
key 6 up
key 9 up
wait 888
tap REC
wait 50
expect take 0
expect mode 1
expect app_loop 9
expect loop_bars9 4
expect loop_ch9_0 916
expect loop_ch9_1 -1
expect loop_ch9_4 500
expect loop_ch9_8 0
expect loop_ch9_12 700
expect loop_ch9_13 -1
expect msg_is_NEW 1
wait 1470
expect loop_now 9
shot 2_verse.png
tap ARP
expect page 4
expect app_loop 9
turn SELECT 1
expect page 5
turn K4 1
expect loop_name9 Verse
wait 50
shot 2_named.png
# ---- 3. Write your chorus: HOME, KNOB 4 to "-" (FREE), REC, C G Am F, REC: L10; name it: ARP, SELECT, NAME: Chorus
tap HOME
expect page 0
turn K4 -9
wait 50
expect mode 0
shot 3_free.png
tap REC
expect take 2
wait 980
key 7 down
key 11 down
key 14 down
wait 100
key 7 up
key 11 up
key 14 up
wait 2288
key 2 down
key 6 down
key 9 down
wait 100
key 2 up
key 6 up
key 9 up
wait 2288
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
wait 100
key 4 up
key 7 up
key 11 up
wait 2288
key 0 down
key 4 down
key 7 down
wait 100
key 0 up
key 4 up
key 7 up
wait 888
tap REC
wait 50
expect take 0
expect mode 1
expect app_loop 10
expect loop_bars10 4
expect loop_ch10_0 0
expect loop_ch10_4 700
expect loop_ch10_8 916
expect loop_ch10_12 500
wait 1470
expect loop_now 10
tap ARP
expect page 4
expect app_loop 10
turn SELECT 1
expect page 5
turn K4 2
expect loop_name10 Chorus
wait 50
shot 3_named.png
# ---- 4. Build the song: HOME, SELECT to SONG; white keys 9, 10, 9, 10: a row each
tap HOME
expect page 0
turn SELECT 1
expect page 1
tapkey w8
tapkey w9
tapkey w8
tapkey w9
expect rows 4
expect row_loop1 9
expect row_loop2 10
expect row_loop3 9
expect row_loop4 10
expect cursor 5
wait 50
shot 4_rows.png
# ---- 5. Shape it: row 2 (a chorus) SECTION Main B (row 4 follows), REPEAT x2; row 4: page 2, KEY +2; a
# breakdown: row 3's drums muted (black 1, 2: D1, D2)
turn K1 -3
expect cursor 2
turn K3 2
expect row_sect2 2
expect row_sect4 2
expect row_sect1 0
expect row_sect3 0
turn K4 1
expect row_rep2 2
turn K1 2
expect cursor 4
turn SELECT 1
expect page 2
turn K1 2
expect row_key4 2
wait 50
shot 5_key.png
turn PRESET -1
expect cursor 3
tapkey b0
tapkey b1
expect row_mute3 3
wait 50
shot 5_shaped.png
# ---- 6. Play it: PLAY on the SONG page; the band is playing L10, so the song comes in from row 1 at the next bar
# line (no Intro: that's from a stop); the rows with fills between sections, the Ending, the stop
tap PLAY
wait 50
expect playing 1
expect msg_is_NEXT 1
expect loop_now 10
# row 1 (Main A) from the bar line (about 2.4 s); its last bar the Fill AB, Main B next
wait 3550
expect mode 2
expect row 1
expect sect 2
expect loop_now 9
wait 50
shot 6_song.png
wait 7150
expect sect 4
expect row 1
# row 2, the chorus, x2 on Main B; the Fill BA in its last bar
wait 2400
expect sect 3
expect row 2
expect loop_now 10
wait 50
shot 6_chorus.png
wait 14350
expect sect 3
expect row 2
wait 2400
expect sect 5
expect row 2
# row 3, the verse without drums (the breakdown); the Fill AB before row 4
wait 2400
expect sect 2
expect row 3
expect mutes 3
wait 7200
expect sect 4
expect row 3
# row 4, the last chorus a tone up: its C plays as D
wait 2400
expect sect 3
expect row 4
expect mutes 0
expect chord_root 2
# the Ending, then the stop
# (not saved yet: Polly saves only at rest, a flash write pauses the audio)
wait 9600
expect sect 6
expect dirty 1
# ---- 7. Save: just stop (here the song stops by itself): Polly saves by itself once the sound has died away
# (and 4 s after your last touch); SAVE saves at once. After a restart: all there
wait 6000
expect playing 0
expect dirty 0
tap SAVE
expect dirty 0
reboot
expect rows 4
expect row_loop2 10
expect row_sect4 2
expect row_rep2 2
expect row_key4 2
expect row_mute3 3
expect loop_name9 Verse
expect loop_name10 Chorus
expect loop_ch9_0 916
expect loop_ch10_0 0
